# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Alexander Gomez
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Super Spectral - target-neutral Kconfig defaults (ESP-IDF v6.0.x, ADR 0001).
# Board-specific flash/PSRAM/CPU settings live in sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3,
# which the build system auto-loads next to this file (do NOT list it in
# SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS). CI overlays: sdkconfig.ci.{qemu,release,analyzer}.
#
# Every symbol below was grepped against ~/.espressif/v6.0.1/esp-idf on
# 2026-08-20 (symbol names, not line numbers - they rot across minors).
# This file only seeds a NEW sdkconfig. After editing:
#   rm -f sdkconfig && idf.py reconfigure     (or idf.py fullclean && idf.py build)
# Regenerate a minimal file from a tuned sdkconfig with: idf.py save-defconfig

# ---- Target pin: a regenerated sdkconfig must never default to plain ESP32 ----
# (discovered 2026-08-21: rm sdkconfig + idf.py build configured esp32 -> 2 MB flash)
CONFIG_IDF_TARGET="esp32s3"

# ---- Reproducibility (docs/devenv/env.lock.md; CI builds twice and diffs) ----
# Selects COMPILER_HIDE_PATHS_MACROS; maps paths to /IDF, /IDF_PROJECT, ...;
# drops timestamps from app + bootloader metadata. GDB then needs
# build/gdbinit/prefix_map (idf.py gdb wires it automatically).
CONFIG_APP_REPRODUCIBLE_BUILD=y

# ---- Partition table (partitions.csv; offsets frozen by ADR 0014) -----------
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions.csv"
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_OFFSET=0x8000

# ---- Anti-brick (ADR 0015): the BOOT button is INSIDE the case --------------
# Rollback: a build that never calls esp_ota_mark_app_valid_cancel_rollback()
# is reverted by the bootloader on the next reset. The bootloader watchdog
# covers the window before app_main.
CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE=y
CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_WDT_ENABLE=y

# ---- NEVER inherit these (asserted by pre-commit; eFuses are read-only) -----
# Secure boot / flash encryption are one-way eFuse burns on a board whose only
# recovery path is USB-Serial-JTAG. Both stay n for the life of the project.
CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT=n
CONFIG_SECURE_FLASH_ENC_ENABLED=n

# ---- Console on native USB-Serial-JTAG (zero exposed GPIO, no UART) ---------
# Must be the PRIMARY console. ESP_CONSOLE_SECONDARY_USB_SERIAL_JTAG is
# output-only and `depends on !ESP_CONSOLE_USB_SERIAL_JTAG`.
# USJ_NO_AUTO_LS_ON_CONNECTION stops automatic light sleep (esp_pm) from
# killing the console while a host is attached.
CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_USB_SERIAL_JTAG=y
CONFIG_USJ_NO_AUTO_LS_ON_CONNECTION=y

# ---- Post-mortem to the 60 KB coredump partition -----------------------------
# In v6.0 the format/checksum choices are gone: ESP_COREDUMP_ENABLE `select`s
# ESP_COREDUMP_DATA_FORMAT_ELF and ESP_COREDUMP_CHECKSUM_SHA256, and neither is
# defined as a `config` anywhere in the v6.0.1 tree - so they are NOT set here
# (an assignment to an undefined symbol only earns a kconfgen warning, but it
# would be a lie in this file). Retrieval: docs/devenv/coredump-runbook.md.
CONFIG_ESP_COREDUMP_ENABLE_TO_FLASH=y

# ---- Floating point / libc --------------------------------------------------
# This product is numeric readouts (Hz, cents, dB): printf("%f") must work.
# In v6.0 the default libc is PICOLIBC, not Newlib: components/esp_libc/Kconfig
# `choice LIBC` defaults to LIBC_PICOLIBC and picks LIBC_NEWLIB only under
# IDF_TOOLCHAIN_CLANG (migration guide release-6.x/6.0/system.rst, "Default
# LibC changed from Newlib to PicolibC"). LIBC_NEWLIB_NANO_FORMAT `depends on
# LIBC_NEWLIB`, so under the default GCC toolchain the line below is INERT -
# kconfgen ignores it. It is kept (harmless) for the clang-toolchain case,
# where Newlib is selected and the nano format would drop float formatting.
# Picolibc's float printf is NOT gated by any Kconfig symbol in the v6.0.1
# tree; the migration guide's own example prints "%.1000f". Confirm at the
# E1 gate build with a printf("%f") smoke test over the USJ console
# (firmware/twatch-s3/README.md, "What comes next", E1 row).
# Note the v6.0 rename: CONFIG_NEWLIB_* -> CONFIG_LIBC_* (components/esp_libc).
CONFIG_LIBC_NEWLIB_NANO_FORMAT=n

# ---- Real-time behaviour ----------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ=1000
# -O2. NEVER add -ffast-math: it breaks golden-file agreement with the host.
CONFIG_COMPILER_OPTIMIZATION_PERF=y
CONFIG_LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL_INFO=y
CONFIG_COMPILER_WARN_WRITE_STRINGS=y
# Deliberately NOT set: CONFIG_COMPILER_DISABLE_GCC*_WARNINGS,
# CONFIG_COMPILER_DISABLE_DEFAULT_ERRORS (v6.0 default is warnings-as-errors;
# keep it). Per-component -Werror -Wshadow -Wconversion -Wdouble-promotion
# -Wformat=2 -Wundef -Wvla live in each components/*/CMakeLists.txt.

# ---- Watchdogs: ON and PANICKING. Fix the design, never the timeout. --------
# A reset is strictly better than a wedge: it gives the ROM bootloader another
# USB enumeration window (ADR 0015). ESP_TASK_WDT_PANIC default is n (log only);
# ESP_TASK_WDT_TIMEOUT_S default is 5.
CONFIG_ESP_INT_WDT=y
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_EN=y
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_INIT=y
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_TIMEOUT_S=10
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_PANIC=y
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_CHECK_IDLE_TASK_CPU0=y
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_CHECK_IDLE_TASK_CPU1=y
CONFIG_FREERTOS_CHECK_STACKOVERFLOW_CANARY=y

# ---- Brownout: keep the LOWEST threshold on a 400-470 mAh cell --------------
# v6.0 location: components/esp_hw_support/power_supply/port/esp32s3/Kconfig.power
# Seven levels SEL_7 (2.44 V, default, lowest) ... SEL_1 (3.30 V). There is
# NO SEL_0 on the S3. The 4.x-era CONFIG_ESP32S3_BROWNOUT_DET_LVL_SEL_* names
# are silently renamed by esp_system/sdkconfig.rename.esp32s3 - do not use them.
CONFIG_ESP_BROWNOUT_DET=y
CONFIG_ESP_BROWNOUT_DET_LVL_SEL_7=y

# ---- No radio in v1 (ADR 0017) ----------------------------------------------
# The real guard is structural: CMakeLists.txt sets `set(COMPONENTS main)`, so
# bt, esp_wifi, esp_netif, lwip, openthread are NOT in the build at all (the
# pre-commit `sdkconfig-invariants` hook asserts that line). Their Kconfig
# symbols therefore do not exist in the generated sdkconfig; the two lines
# below are kept for intent and are harmlessly ignored (2026-08-21: verified
# that the trimmed build drops CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_ENABLED, which is promptless
# and could not have been set to n any other way). SX1262 stays in reset with
# ALDO4 off.
CONFIG_BT_ENABLED=n
